preConditionHook:
// VolumeBelowAverageFraction -- Brooks (T06-24, slice 14). Folded into
// VolumeBelowAverage as a volumeFraction input 2026-09-13; split back out as its
// own rule 2026-09-27 so VolumeBelowAverage stays the plain below-average test.
//
// The bar's volume is below volumeFraction times its own N-bar average volume,
// window INCLUSIVE of the current bar -- Brooks's "quiet, low-volume market" gate.
// Brooks says only that volume is low, so 0.8 over 20 bars is a reading, which is
// why both are inputs. volume is EasyLanguage's UP-TICK count: this is an up-tick
// RATIO, the same series VolumeBelowAverage measures. At volumeFraction = 1 it is
// VolumeBelowAverage exactly.
avgVolume = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)lookback; ++i) {
    avgVolume += (double)volume[i];
}
avgVolume /= (int)lookback;
